From 92b4f993dca8b145c47deb114434202233547726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:59:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] multitenant: measure per-tenant cost with governance
 plugin (SQLite)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the spike with a third loader that opens a per-tenant SQLite
configstore and constructs the plugins/governance plugin against it.
This is the worst-case isolation model — each tenant gets its own DB
file with its own GORM connection pool — which lets us upper-bound the
per-tenant residency cost.

Per-tenant heap delta: 31.7 KiB (telemetry) → 876 KiB (governance).
Cold-start: 152 us → 65 ms. Goroutines: 5 → 7 (governance starts
background reset workers).

The 65 ms cold-start is dominated by AutoMigrate on a fresh DB; an
already-migrated tenant DB would be single-digit ms.

go.mod adds plugins/governance v1.5.18 and framework v1.3.18; both at
the same published versions other modules use. The workspace go.work
resolves cross-module imports locally.

SPIKE_FINDINGS.md now compares all three configurations side-by-side.
**Phase 1 design constraint locked in**: the configstore must be
shared across tenants with tenant_id row scoping. Per-tenant DB files
do not scale past ~1000 tenants (10k × 900 KiB = 9 GiB heap, 70k
goroutines). Per-tenant connection pools should NOT be the default.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
