 ## Headline numbers (indicative, NOT a benchmark)
 
-| Metric | No plugins | With telemetry plugin |
-|---|---|---|
-| Cold-start `Acquire→Init` (avg) | 22–87 µs | 152–195 µs |
-| Per-tenant heap (avg, 3 tenants) | ~8.6 KiB | ~31.7 KiB |
-| Per-tenant goroutines | 5 | 5 |
-| LRU eviction + Acquire #4 | ~50 µs | — |
-| VK resolve, cached | 42 ns/op | — |
-| VK resolve, uncached | 3 ns/op | — |
-| Manager.Shutdown | 20 µs | 24 µs |
-
-Configuration used per tenant: `Concurrency=4`, `BufferSize=16`,
-`InitialPoolSize=32`. No MCP. The telemetry pass loads `plugins/telemetry`
-with a fresh `*prometheus.Registry` per tenant; ~20 metric vectors get
-registered each time.
-
-**Reading the delta:** telemetry alone adds ~23 KiB per tenant (3× the
-no-plugin baseline) and ~3× the cold-start latency. Extrapolating to 10k
-tenants × telemetry-only = ~320 MiB heap, ~50k goroutines — tractable on
-a modern host. Cost will grow ~linearly as each additional plugin loads.
+| Metric | No plugins | + telemetry | + governance (SQLite) |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Cold-start `Acquire→Init` (avg) | 22–87 µs | 152–195 µs | **65 ms** |
+| Per-tenant heap (avg, 3 tenants) | ~8.6 KiB | ~31.7 KiB | **~876 KiB** |
+| Per-tenant goroutines | 5 | 5 | **7** |
+| LRU eviction + Acquire #4 | ~50 µs | — | — |
+| VK resolve, cached | 42 ns/op | — | — |
+| Manager.Shutdown | 20 µs | 24 µs | 27 µs |
+
+Configuration: `Concurrency=4`, `BufferSize=16`, `InitialPoolSize=32`,
+no MCP. The governance pass opens a fresh SQLite file per tenant in a
+temp dir and runs schema migrations on every Init — this is the
+**worst-case isolation model** (per-tenant DB). The realistic Phase 1
+design shares one Postgres with `tenant_id` FKs, which will be much
+cheaper per tenant but loses crash isolation.
+
+**Reading the deltas:**
+
+- Telemetry alone: +23 KiB / tenant, ~3× cold-start. Tractable to ~10k tenants.
+- Governance alone (per-tenant SQLite): +870 KiB / tenant, ~30,000× cold-start.
+  10k tenants × 900 KiB = ~9 GiB heap. **Not** tractable in this isolation
+  model. Cold-start of 65 ms is dominated by `AutoMigrate` on a fresh DB;
+  on a pre-existing tenant DB this drops to single-digit ms.
+
+**Critical implication for Phase 1:** the realistic SaaS design must share
+the underlying GORM connection pool across tenants. Per-tenant DB files
+(or per-tenant schemas) don't scale past ~1000 tenants. This pushes toward
+the documented Phase 1 plan: one Postgres + `tenant_id` FK on every
+governance table + a shared `configstore.ConfigStore` whose query layer
+scopes by tenant. Per-tenant connection pools should NOT be the default.
 
